+# Vaultr Extensions (`vaultr-exts`) 🧩
+> Modular sub-extensions catalog for Vaultr (the AnyMD vault and remote storage manager).
+
+Loaded dynamically in Vaultr's extension interface via GitHub raw manifests or the central registry catalog: [`registry/extensions.json`](file:///home/antigravity/t3hkitty/vaultr-exts/registry/extensions.json).
+
+---
+
+## Catalog of Sub-Extensions
+
+| Extension ID | Category | Description | Capabilities |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| **`vaultr-pandoc-converter`** | `converter` | Pandoc-based multi-format document conversion pipeline (epub, md, html, docx, pdf) preserving `.anymd` sidecar metadata and tags. | `pandoc-conversion`, `sidecar-metadata-preserve` |
+| **`vaultr-movr-organizer`** | `organizer` | Taxonomy rule-based file organizer moving files into clean hierarchies with `rclone moveto` dry-run plans and sidecar path tracking. | `rule-based-organize`, `sidecar-path-migration`, `rclone-move-plan` |
+| **`vaultr-content-tagger`** | `tagger` | Auto-evaluates tags based on file extensions, path structure, and sidecar text corpus without touching core media binaries. | `auto-tagging`, `sidecar-tag-sync` |
+| **`vaultr-kittlibr-metadata`** | `metadata` | Bridges rich book and document YAML metadata from Kittlibr into AnyMD sidecars with symlink and cross-index support. | `kittlibr-schema-sync`, `yaml-sidecar-enrichment`, `symlink-sidecar` |
+| **`vaultr-backup-manifest`** | `backup` | Archive and backup orchestrator generating `.manifests/*.anymd` sidecars with MD5 checksum verification and `rclone copy --files-from` pipelines. | `archive-creation`, `sidecar-manifest-verify`, `md5-backup-audit` |
+| **`vaultr-md5-dedupe`** | `dedupe` | Safe MD5 duplicate clustering, keeper selection, and non-destructive quarantine workflows. | `md5-deduplication`, `quarantine-preview`, `safe-resolution` |
+
+---
+
+## Cross-Platform File Manager Vision
+
+Vaultr is designed to function seamlessly across:
+- **Android**: Interfacing with the Android Document Chooser (SAF storage access).
+- **Windows**: Windows File Manager mounts (`Z:\`, `T:\`).
+- **Cloud & Remotes**: Surgical `rclone` endpoints (`davjump:`, `koofr:`, `tbox:`, `meow-vault`).
+- **Web / GitHub Pages**: Standalone pure HTML/JS bundle for AnyMD.
+
+---
+
+## Development & Test
+
+```bash
+npm install
+npm run build
+npm test
+```
